WEBVTT

00:05.920 --> 00:11.150
This Elements changes its shape according
to the minds of those who challenge me.

00:11.530 --> 00:15.150
It's the first time the Casino of the Gods
has ever been projected onto it.

00:16.900 --> 00:18.300
Are you Gremoire?

00:18.660 --> 00:19.920
Correct.

00:19.920 --> 00:22.610
I analyze the information from
the moment humans visit me,

00:22.610 --> 00:26.460
down to their physical appearance and Arise.

00:26.460 --> 00:29.520
But I couldn't capture yours.

00:29.520 --> 00:32.430
I'm more surprised by your appearance.

00:32.430 --> 00:36.620
This appearance was chosen by someone
who had only recently been transformed.

00:36.620 --> 00:39.850
And now, the name of
this game is "Three Cheats."

00:40.850 --> 00:42.940
TWO SIDES OF A COIN
Two sides of a coin.

00:43.380 --> 00:45.020
POKER
Poker.

00:45.620 --> 00:48.240
OLD MAID
Old maid. And with all these games...

00:48.690 --> 00:50.200
...I'm going to win.

00:52.700 --> 00:54.200
So you're going to cheat, huh?

00:55.160 --> 01:00.100
Yes, this game is to find out
the cheat I'm going to set up.

01:00.590 --> 01:02.540
And an important promise:

01:02.900 --> 01:06.390
I only use one type of cheat.

01:07.650 --> 01:09.790
Oh? Interesting.

01:09.790 --> 01:13.720
I'll tell your friends about my cheat first.

01:14.210 --> 01:17.930
If you're all understanding that,
then let's start the game.

01:18.400 --> 01:20.220
Such confidence you have.

01:20.220 --> 01:22.400
Okay, I'll listen.

01:26.400 --> 01:28.820
My "cheat" is...

01:32.640 --> 01:33.510
Huh?

01:33.510 --> 01:34.780
- What?
- What's that?!

01:36.160 --> 01:37.870
This is going to be fun.

01:37.870 --> 01:39.550
You can trust Fay.

01:39.550 --> 01:41.580
I'm sure he'll see through it.

01:41.940 --> 01:43.240
I believe in you!

01:44.100 --> 01:46.290
So, good luck with that.

01:46.710 --> 01:49.260
The three cheats from god...

01:49.640 --> 01:51.850
...can you spot them?

01:53.390 --> 01:55.410
I'm up for that game.

02:25.460 --> 02:27.130
GODS' GAME WE PLAY

02:28.500 --> 02:33.800
GODS' GAME WE PLAY

03:27.560 --> 03:32.440
PLAYER.10: THREE CHEATS
THAT COME FROM GOD

03:32.860 --> 03:33.750
THE THREE CHEATS

03:33.750 --> 03:34.860
WIN CONDITION:

03:34.860 --> 03:36.040
TO FIND OUT THE CHEAT THAT
LED GOD TO A CERTAIN VICTORY

03:36.040 --> 03:37.050
LOSE CONDITION

03:37.050 --> 03:37.860
FAILURE TO FIND OUT GOD'S CHEAT

03:38.660 --> 03:40.680
Let's start with the first game,

03:40.680 --> 03:43.330
two sides of the coin.

03:43.650 --> 03:45.800
Choose the coin you want to use.

03:45.800 --> 03:47.650
Then, I'll choose a black and white coin.

03:55.700 --> 03:58.210
Am I the coin-tosser? Or you?

03:58.210 --> 04:03.810
To make this fair, all three games will be
played by your friends as dealers.

04:03.810 --> 04:05.510
Let's start with you.

04:07.370 --> 04:09.430
I don't feel like doing it,

04:09.430 --> 04:12.480
but I'll be the dealer then.

04:15.200 --> 04:16.390
What are you doing?

04:16.940 --> 04:18.800
My role is the coin toss.

04:18.800 --> 04:21.620
I'll toss this coin beautifully.

04:21.620 --> 04:25.930
I have to practice my kicking
because my Arise uses feet.

04:25.930 --> 04:27.160
I see.

04:27.160 --> 04:29.930
The face of Master Fay,
white is the head

04:29.930 --> 04:31.240
and black is the reverse.

04:31.240 --> 04:32.630
The procedure is:

04:32.920 --> 04:34.500
I kick the coin up.

04:34.500 --> 04:36.680
While the coin is in the air,

04:36.680 --> 04:39.090
Master Fay chooses
the sides of the coin.

04:39.090 --> 04:43.100
After that declaration,
I kicked it up again to make it fair.

04:43.100 --> 04:45.970
It's settled on the reverse side or
face once the coin is dropped.

04:47.030 --> 04:49.270
Now, I'll begin!

04:52.090 --> 04:55.120
Once the coin has flown into the air,
no blatant trick is possible.

04:55.530 --> 04:58.190
Furthermore, I have the right to
choose the sides of the coin.

04:58.190 --> 04:59.710
So the cheat is

04:59.710 --> 05:03.120
that it makes it impossible for me
to guess the side of the coin.

05:04.240 --> 05:05.050
Head!

05:11.370 --> 05:12.330
It's the reverse...

05:12.710 --> 05:14.230
I'm sorry, Master Fay.

05:14.590 --> 05:16.410
You don't need to apologize.

05:16.840 --> 05:19.150
There were no unnatural moves from her.

05:19.150 --> 05:22.500
It looks as if she will lose by accident
if she fails to guess the coin.

05:22.870 --> 05:25.050
So the cheat is really there.

05:26.760 --> 05:29.630
All right, let's move on to game two.

05:29.630 --> 05:33.160
Why such a hurry?
Is that impatience?

05:33.160 --> 05:36.480
Chief Miranda is waiting for us
to come back.

05:37.680 --> 05:41.180
Now, the next game is poker,
which doesn't use coins.

05:41.180 --> 05:44.820
You can only exchange once from
your initial hand of five cards.

05:45.190 --> 05:47.180
After that, the game concluded.

05:47.180 --> 05:49.020
So it's a total game of luck.

05:49.020 --> 05:52.230
"A must-win."
It's that kind of cheat.

05:52.230 --> 05:53.400
And the dealer is...

05:53.400 --> 05:54.880
Me!

05:57.450 --> 05:59.760
The cards are in order.

05:59.760 --> 06:02.470
There doesn't seem to be any mark
or pattern on these cards.

06:02.470 --> 06:05.090
The cheat is common in all three games.

06:05.090 --> 06:09.640
If the coin earlier had a trick,
then this poker also had one.

06:09.640 --> 06:12.640
But when Leshea doesn't notice it,

06:12.640 --> 06:15.790
it's unlikely that her power
is interfering with this game.

06:19.710 --> 06:23.380
Two pairs, huh?
I also got the strongest ace.

06:23.830 --> 06:25.580
From here, if I exchange sevens

06:25.580 --> 06:29.210
for eights or an ace, I am almost
guaranteed to win with a full house.

06:30.290 --> 06:34.610
How about your hand?
Hopefully you got strong cards.

06:34.610 --> 06:36.810
Which one of us exchanges hands first?

06:37.210 --> 06:38.250
Whatever.

06:38.800 --> 06:41.140
Then I'll do it first.

06:41.140 --> 06:42.170
I changed five cards.

06:42.590 --> 06:43.720
- Eh?!
- What?

06:43.720 --> 06:45.680
What are you doing, Master Fay?!

06:45.680 --> 06:49.130
That's right!
You already had two pair!

06:49.130 --> 06:51.210
If I change one card,

06:51.210 --> 06:54.190
the second and later cards in the pile
go to the god's hand.

06:54.190 --> 06:55.990
I'll use this all change

06:55.990 --> 06:57.960
to see if there are any cheats there.

06:58.360 --> 06:59.820
Then I'll give them out.

07:03.190 --> 07:06.710
One pair.
No overt tricks were spotted.

07:07.340 --> 07:08.700
What's your exchange?

07:11.160 --> 07:13.280
Straight flush.

07:14.000 --> 07:15.830
That's too obvious.

07:15.830 --> 07:19.710
Now, I must think of a cheat that
coin-guessing and poker have in common.

07:20.400 --> 07:22.030
Is there object manipulation?

07:22.030 --> 07:25.460
No, that doesn't explain
the straight flush.

07:26.500 --> 07:29.130
Let's proceed to the old maid.

07:31.350 --> 07:33.710
All right, go on.

07:40.150 --> 07:42.280
I'm too nervous!

07:42.280 --> 07:44.810
There are no tricks
on any of the cards.

07:45.470 --> 07:48.640
Here are 27 and 26 cards,

07:48.640 --> 07:51.830
but if you have a pair,
you can place them on the table.

07:52.540 --> 07:54.040
27 cards?

07:54.480 --> 07:57.290
I have one more card
than her, huh?

08:05.780 --> 08:09.580
I'll let you choose your turn since you
have the most cards in your hand.

08:10.890 --> 08:12.850
Leftmost from me.

08:16.310 --> 08:18.200
Then it's my turn.

08:18.200 --> 08:20.190
By the way, you are there.

08:20.190 --> 08:21.100
Yes?

08:21.100 --> 08:23.440
What are you trying to do?

08:23.770 --> 08:26.230
You want this human to win, don't you?

08:26.230 --> 08:27.530
It's a service.

08:28.100 --> 08:31.540
You should be right behind me,
so I can't cheat.

08:31.540 --> 08:32.950
Eh?

08:33.360 --> 08:35.290
What are you planning to do?

08:35.290 --> 08:38.910
I choose to play fair games.
That's my style.

08:38.910 --> 08:41.310
Are there any cards
that look suspicious to you?

08:42.010 --> 08:46.010
No, there are not. I didn't find
any cheats on the cards.

08:46.370 --> 08:48.860
It was my turn to draw the cards, wasn't it?

08:49.840 --> 08:51.990
This is unexpected.

08:51.990 --> 08:55.560
I thought it was a cheat
who avoided all my jokers.

08:55.860 --> 08:58.170
Coincidence? Or is she going for it?

08:58.170 --> 09:01.390
You know, the joker is in my hand.

09:01.390 --> 09:03.140
It's your turn to draw.

09:03.140 --> 09:04.330
Card on the left.

09:07.990 --> 09:09.950
Then it's my turn.

09:13.410 --> 09:15.060
Overwhelming advantage.

09:15.520 --> 09:17.780
If I draw a 3 or a 9 here, I win.

09:17.780 --> 09:20.370
The probability of winning is 66.6%.

09:20.750 --> 09:22.610
As long as I don't draw a joker...

09:24.620 --> 09:25.960
Card on the right.

09:27.970 --> 09:28.700
Huh?

09:29.010 --> 09:30.490
Did she let me draw it?

09:30.490 --> 09:33.920
Unless she has precognition,
she can't place it in advance!

09:33.920 --> 09:37.830
But that means she can't win on
the two sides of coins and poker.

09:38.930 --> 09:40.640
I'm choosing the right too.

09:42.640 --> 09:46.850
Okay, if you take this next turn, I'll win.

09:47.360 --> 09:51.860
I won all three games, as promised.

09:51.860 --> 09:54.320
Now answer me...

09:54.770 --> 09:56.880
Where is my cheat?

09:58.830 --> 10:00.450
My opponent is a god.

10:01.890 --> 10:03.000
They can do anything.

10:06.670 --> 10:09.050
- Hey!
- What's that?!

10:09.390 --> 10:14.970
But will we find out the cheats
that humans can't even handle?

10:14.970 --> 10:16.760
And one more thing,

10:16.760 --> 10:18.970
I felt something strange
when I played old maid.

10:21.180 --> 10:23.730
She couldn't see through my joker.

10:24.190 --> 10:25.970
It's clearly a cheat,

10:25.970 --> 10:28.100
but in that moment,
there was a gap.

10:28.730 --> 10:32.630
I must remember everything
that happened in this game.

10:41.180 --> 10:42.410
Let's do it again.

10:43.260 --> 10:44.880
I'll take my revenge on the old maid.

10:45.800 --> 10:48.290
Pearl, deliver the cards again.

10:48.290 --> 10:52.220
You can't spot the cheat,
and you're just trying to buy time, huh?

10:52.220 --> 10:53.170
No.

10:54.010 --> 10:56.870
I'll beat you in the next game.

10:57.970 --> 11:00.970
GODS' GAME WE PLAY

11:04.360 --> 11:08.270
Do you mind if I draw first because I have
more cards in my hand like before?

11:08.270 --> 11:09.770
Yes, go ahead.

11:09.770 --> 11:10.880
Left.

11:13.990 --> 11:15.820
Second from the right.

11:22.630 --> 11:24.080
What's the matter with you?

11:24.080 --> 11:26.330
Why are you staring at me like that?

11:27.220 --> 11:28.100
Right.

11:31.170 --> 11:33.320
Then I'll choose this.

11:36.030 --> 11:37.760
Oh, that's too bad.

11:38.230 --> 11:40.670
Do you think you're lucky?

11:40.670 --> 11:44.670
It looks like you win if you
draw a five from me,

11:44.670 --> 11:47.860
but it's just the same game as before.

11:48.230 --> 11:50.270
It's the joker you'll draw.

11:50.690 --> 11:53.650
No, God's victory is broken.

11:54.090 --> 11:55.730
It's time to compare the answers!

11:56.390 --> 11:57.150
Right!

12:00.640 --> 12:05.250
My cheating is working!
You should definitely draw joker!

12:05.590 --> 12:06.430
Fay!

12:06.430 --> 12:07.960
That was close.

12:09.210 --> 12:11.450
The cheat is an accomplice.

12:11.450 --> 12:13.670
Between you and my friends.

12:15.510 --> 12:17.590
It was four against one here.

12:17.590 --> 12:19.290
You weren't the one.

12:19.290 --> 12:20.850
I was the one.

12:21.490 --> 12:22.680
Right, Leshea?

12:22.680 --> 12:26.140
You're right.
So you knew it.

12:26.140 --> 12:28.520
Did you suspect Nel and Pearl?

12:28.520 --> 12:31.150
I-It's not my fault.

12:31.150 --> 12:32.950
How did you know?

12:33.530 --> 12:35.230
You drew the wrong card.

12:35.230 --> 12:36.930
At this point, I could guess that

12:36.930 --> 12:40.280
the winning strategy is definitely the system
that makes me draw the joker.

12:41.070 --> 12:45.500
In other words, the cheat is only triggered
if there is a joker in your hand.

12:46.340 --> 12:50.870
On the contrary, the god
can't cheat on Fay's hand.

12:50.870 --> 12:55.350
That's right. So, here was
the key to my discomfort.

12:55.350 --> 12:56.210
Pearl,

12:56.540 --> 12:58.760
why did you give me 27 cards?

12:58.760 --> 12:59.550
Huh?

13:00.010 --> 13:03.160
Here are 27 and 26 cards...

13:03.760 --> 13:06.730
I had 27 cards, one more than god.

13:07.410 --> 13:10.860
That hand disadvantaged me in two games.

13:11.290 --> 13:14.820
It started when my friends had
a suspicion, and I realized it.

13:15.400 --> 13:18.190
Pearl always stood behind you.

13:18.190 --> 13:21.530
Right, she disguises her ability while
monitoring the cards in your hand.

13:21.860 --> 13:24.220
That's her Arise to swap the card.

13:24.700 --> 13:28.320
The moment I drew a card,
she used Shift Change.

13:29.170 --> 13:31.810
Once I figured out your work,
the rest was easy.

13:32.270 --> 13:36.080
Nel and Leshea cheated on
two sides of coins and poker, too.

13:36.820 --> 13:38.570
But I was amazed.

13:38.570 --> 13:42.630
You've given us a hint of the trick
from the very beginning, right?

13:42.940 --> 13:45.510
I analyze the information from
the moment humans visit me,

13:45.510 --> 13:49.850
down to their physical appearance and Arise.

13:50.200 --> 13:52.810
You already knew about
Pearl and Nel's abilities,

13:53.480 --> 13:57.270
and you told them at the time
to help you cheat.

13:58.020 --> 13:59.280
I'm sorry.

13:59.280 --> 14:01.810
I don't want to cheat like that,

14:01.810 --> 14:04.070
but I manipulated the rotation with my Arise.

14:05.430 --> 14:06.080
Yeah.

14:06.710 --> 14:07.830
At that moment,

14:07.830 --> 14:12.020
Nel activated the moment reversal
so that the back side would appear.

14:12.580 --> 14:14.250
I'm really sorry!

14:14.790 --> 14:17.320
I don't need to explain
Leshea's part, so I'll skip it.

14:17.320 --> 14:18.300
Why?!

14:18.760 --> 14:22.550
Because in the poker game, you're a dealer
and don't have to do anything, right?

14:23.440 --> 14:26.410
I can make a straight flush
on my first hand of poker

14:26.410 --> 14:28.260
with my eyes closed.

14:28.580 --> 14:30.010
What do you think, Gremoire?

14:30.010 --> 14:32.960
I still don't understand
the last old maid.

14:32.960 --> 14:37.480
Even if you'd seen through my cheat,
it's impossible for you to win.

14:37.820 --> 14:39.080
You're right.

14:39.610 --> 14:42.820
Pearl's Shift Change is usually unstoppable.

14:43.260 --> 14:44.280
Violating the rules?

14:44.720 --> 14:47.400
You broke the rule on
activating Arise, didn't you?

14:47.400 --> 14:49.930
No. She couldn't activate it.

14:51.360 --> 14:55.460
I have to have touched the object within
three minutes before I can replace it.

14:55.460 --> 14:58.390
It had been more than three minutes
since the cards were handed out.

14:58.390 --> 14:59.420
Hence,

14:59.420 --> 15:01.730
the Shift Change could not be triggered.

15:02.420 --> 15:04.260
Y-Yes! That's it!

15:05.200 --> 15:06.720
Stalling for time?

15:06.720 --> 15:08.610
That observation is a bluff!

15:08.610 --> 15:10.920
But you finally make 50:50.

15:10.920 --> 15:13.380
It was mere luck that you
were able to pull a 5.

15:13.380 --> 15:14.940
You're wrong.

15:14.940 --> 15:18.050
You didn't change your
joker's position, did you?

15:18.810 --> 15:22.320
Normally, when you draw a joker,
you shuffle it,

15:22.320 --> 15:23.270
but you didn't.

15:26.630 --> 15:28.610
I trust Shift Change.

15:34.000 --> 15:36.560
I'm surprised.
It's my loss.

15:36.560 --> 15:38.460
I'll give you the promised reward.

15:40.990 --> 15:41.750
Huh?

15:44.580 --> 15:46.130
Okay, it's done.

15:47.590 --> 15:51.050
Are we really making a comeback?

15:51.400 --> 15:54.050
There's just one more thing left to answer.

15:54.050 --> 15:57.140
You said it was all in your calculation

15:57.140 --> 16:00.590
and you already win no matter
how it turns out, right?

16:01.020 --> 16:03.250
All three of you, show your right hands.

16:07.520 --> 16:09.010
Same number?

16:09.010 --> 16:11.450
Yes, it's an adjustment to our win.

16:12.020 --> 16:14.450
Everyone's winning numbers are equal to 3.

16:16.040 --> 16:17.550
Why would you do that?

16:17.550 --> 16:20.210
I want all of us to win 10 games
at the same time.

16:20.210 --> 16:22.540
We're all friends,
so our goal is the same.

16:22.540 --> 16:24.840
If Nel wins, that's a great result.

16:24.840 --> 16:27.780
If she loses, we've all got
our winning records.

16:29.480 --> 16:31.520
I see. That was fun.

16:32.190 --> 16:35.000
You may reach Clear
on the gods' game,

16:35.000 --> 16:36.730
but you may come back again.

16:40.810 --> 16:43.990
VS GREMOIRE, GOD OF MANY PHASES
WON IN 27 MINUTES AND 1 SECOND,

16:43.990 --> 16:45.690
WITH NEL LOSING HER THREE LOSSES
COMEBACK

16:46.560 --> 16:48.900
Congratulations on your comeback!

16:48.900 --> 16:51.370
T-Thank you!

16:51.370 --> 16:54.870
Four-player games
are the essence of board games.

16:54.870 --> 16:56.820
That's a great number of people!

16:56.820 --> 16:58.670
When four people eat together,

16:58.670 --> 17:01.330
there's a greater sense of
team unity, isn't there?

17:01.330 --> 17:05.580
I'm glad you welcomed me, but have you
reported to the Chief Secretary?

17:06.030 --> 17:08.130
Well, she's a bit busy right now.

17:08.130 --> 17:11.590
That's not good! We're here
to report Nel's return!

17:11.910 --> 17:14.720
Oh, by the way, I got a call.

17:14.720 --> 17:16.680
She said it was something urgent.

17:17.270 --> 17:18.270
MEETING IN PROGRESS

17:18.980 --> 17:21.980
Miranda. You wanted to see us, didn't you?

17:22.700 --> 17:25.770
Here it is Chief Secretary! The request
from the supervising department!

17:25.770 --> 17:27.190
Let's enter.

17:29.470 --> 17:30.660
You guys...

17:31.960 --> 17:33.670
We have trouble now.

17:33.670 --> 17:34.100
URGENT CASE: THE GAME OF NO RETURN

17:34.100 --> 17:35.130
URGENT CASE: THE GAME OF NO RETURN
Over 200 apostles

17:35.130 --> 17:36.140
THERE ARE 209 APOSTLES WHO HAVE DIVED
were forcibly assembled in a huge labyrinth,

17:36.140 --> 17:37.080
FROM ALL OVER THE WORLD. NO ONE HAS RETURNED.
were forcibly assembled in a huge labyrinth,

17:37.080 --> 17:38.050
were forcibly assembled in a huge labyrinth,

17:38.050 --> 17:41.830
and it's been 57 hours,
but none of them have returned.

17:41.830 --> 17:43.790
They can't return to the real world?

17:43.790 --> 17:48.010
And there, HQ panicked and decided
to dispatch a rescue team.

17:48.380 --> 17:51.840
Your team was chosen
for the Ruin Branch.

17:51.840 --> 17:56.560
If you are defeated, you usually
come back to the real world, right?

17:56.950 --> 18:00.500
It seems that in this game, you can try
it again as many times as you want.

18:00.500 --> 18:01.020
Huh?

18:01.020 --> 18:02.950
You can die as many times as you want,

18:02.950 --> 18:05.350
but each time you start over
from the beginning,

18:05.350 --> 18:08.110
it's a respawn.

18:08.110 --> 18:12.290
Isn't that system giving
the human side a certain win?

18:12.290 --> 18:15.700
If you start over, you can escape
that labyrinth at some point.

18:16.140 --> 18:20.040
This infinite respawn is not
a privilege, but an obligation.

18:20.040 --> 18:23.510
In other words, you can't return
to reality until you have completed

18:23.510 --> 18:25.130
this ultra-difficult game.

18:25.130 --> 18:27.280
There are two ways to rescue them:

18:27.280 --> 18:29.460
You have to complete this game.

18:29.460 --> 18:34.340
And the other is to find
a save item in the labyrinth.

18:34.340 --> 18:38.210
If you can't do that,
everyone will be unable to return.

18:38.210 --> 18:42.020
I'm curious. This one is really different
from the previous games.

18:42.500 --> 18:43.990
About the infinite respawns?

18:44.380 --> 18:49.070
No, it's another forced gathering
that's happening on a global scale.

18:49.070 --> 18:50.290
You're right.

18:50.290 --> 18:52.570
I don't remember Apostles
from all over the world

18:52.570 --> 18:54.780
being gathered into one game.

18:55.620 --> 18:58.040
I want to find out
what god's true intentions are.

18:58.040 --> 18:59.580
If we don't know the reason,

18:59.580 --> 19:03.750
it could create the same kind of forced
assembly game over and over again.

19:03.750 --> 19:08.270
But your first priority
is to find the save item.

19:08.270 --> 19:10.910
First of all, we must help those
who are unable to return.

19:10.910 --> 19:11.710
Yes.

19:13.420 --> 19:14.750
VS ??? (GOD)
It's not the full explanation, right?

19:14.750 --> 19:16.050
LABYRINTH ESCAPE GAME
It's not the full explanation, right?

19:16.050 --> 19:16.750
WIN CONDITION:
I can't wait to see how big the maze is.

19:16.750 --> 19:17.450
DEFEAT THE LAST BOSS
I can't wait to see how big the maze is.

19:17.450 --> 19:18.910
AT THE FAR END OF THE LABYRINTH
I can't wait to see how big the maze is.

19:18.910 --> 19:21.250
LOSE CONDITION:
A game of no return?

19:21.250 --> 19:22.520
NONE (INSTEAD, RETIRING IS NOT ALLOWED)
Could it be that we will...

19:22.520 --> 19:23.910
ADDITIONAL RULE:
We'll make it and come back alive!

19:23.910 --> 19:24.890
THERE IS A SAVE ITEM
We'll make it and come back alive!

19:24.890 --> 19:25.770
FOR RETURNING TO THE REAL WORLD
We'll make it and come back alive!

19:25.770 --> 19:26.310
FOR RETURNING TO THE REAL WORLD

19:26.310 --> 19:28.340
This is an unprecedented case.

19:28.340 --> 19:31.710
Fay, I'm sorry to ask you again
after facing Bookmaker.

19:32.590 --> 19:34.900
I'm just doing what I always do.

19:34.900 --> 19:37.190
Playing the game against god.

19:46.210 --> 19:47.670
CHOOSE THE DUNGEON DIFFICULTY LEVEL
Choose difficulty...

19:47.670 --> 19:48.200
1. YOU CAN FEEL LOVE

19:48.200 --> 19:49.460
2. PMD
PMD is...

19:49.460 --> 19:51.580
PLAYER MUST DIE
...Player Must Die.

19:51.580 --> 19:52.420
PLAYER MUST DIE
What?

19:52.830 --> 19:54.010
'You may die,'

19:54.010 --> 19:57.420
which means you have two choices:
a mode that's so easy that you even love it,

19:57.420 --> 20:00.640
or an extremely hard difficulty level
that's trying to kill the player.

20:00.640 --> 20:03.100
That difficulty is too extreme!

20:03.100 --> 20:04.330
Of course, I'll choose this!

20:04.330 --> 20:05.600
Me too!

20:07.840 --> 20:10.390
Hey! What are both thinking?!

20:10.390 --> 20:12.110
We'll choose this.

20:13.440 --> 20:16.440
We might not be able to return to reality!

20:16.440 --> 20:19.020
The ending might diverge
with each difficulty level.

20:20.110 --> 20:22.050
There is a possibility that the ending

20:22.050 --> 20:25.410
where you can return to the real world
is only set in difficult mode.

20:25.410 --> 20:27.100
So I want to make sure of it.

20:27.100 --> 20:30.030
The difficulty settings have been completed.

20:30.590 --> 20:32.500
Welcome to the adventure.

20:33.060 --> 20:36.440
It's time to start your epic
labyrinth exploration.

20:36.930 --> 20:39.570
Huh? What are these numbers?

20:39.570 --> 20:41.120
It disappeared.

20:41.120 --> 20:43.190
Could it be the number of respawns?

20:56.440 --> 20:58.200
It's so peaceful.

20:58.200 --> 21:00.530
Is this the inside of a labyrinth?

21:00.530 --> 21:02.600
No, don't let your guard down!

21:02.600 --> 21:06.870
There must be a trap
disguised in this tranquility!

21:08.070 --> 21:08.750
Oh?

21:09.370 --> 21:13.230
It would be fun to have lunch in that shade.

21:13.230 --> 21:16.080
I should have brought sandwiches.

21:16.080 --> 21:18.050
You're letting your
guard down right away.

21:18.410 --> 21:21.310
Because it's really peaceful here.

21:21.310 --> 21:25.020
Yeah, we still have a long way to go.
I think we could take a short break

21:25.020 --> 21:26.600
for a strategy meeting.

21:26.600 --> 21:28.560
I agree!

21:29.330 --> 21:32.060
Wow, that apple looks delicious!

21:32.400 --> 21:36.020
Apple? It's too big to be a cherry, but...

21:36.020 --> 21:38.110
Don't think about something complicated.

21:38.110 --> 21:42.070
If it's this red, it's definitely
sweet and delicious.

21:42.780 --> 21:43.740
Watch out!

21:48.730 --> 21:50.030
Respawn.

21:52.250 --> 21:53.360
Pearl...

21:53.360 --> 21:55.500
Is it my fault?!

21:55.900 --> 21:58.340
I see. So this is how the game is played.

21:58.650 --> 22:01.820
This is going to take a lot of work.

22:04.190 --> 22:07.430
Ah, I'm free again.

22:08.010 --> 22:12.030
How many decades will it take
until the next human arrives?

22:15.450 --> 22:18.500
Well, what a very unusual
visitor I had today.

22:18.910 --> 22:22.400
You, who tend to keep
to your own world,

22:22.400 --> 22:26.030
what kind of change of mind is it
for you to come here, Uroboros?

22:26.950 --> 22:29.520
Where did those humans go?
